# Line endings, pinned — because a diff nobody can read is a review nobody does.
#
# The pipeline writes tracked artifacts from Python (`models/saved_models/
# metrics.json` via models/train.py, `README.md`'s generated Results block via
# models/report.py). Python's text mode translates "\n" to the platform's
# terminator, so the same file written on Windows and on Linux differs on every
# single line. A retrain that moved one number then shows up as a 1,900-line
# diff, and the number that actually changed is invisible inside it.
#
# Those two writers now pass newline="\n" explicitly. This file is the second
# half of the fix: it covers everything git touches regardless of which tool or
# editor wrote it, so the repository always stores LF and `git diff` always
# shows only what someone meant to change.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never newline-translate a booster. XGBoost's saved model is a binary blob;
# rewriting byte 0x0A inside it produces a file that either fails to load or,
# worse, loads into a different model than the one that was evaluated.
*.xgb binary
*.ubj binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
